<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄτλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>suffering, distress, arising
			from</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδείας ὄτλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφείων ὄτλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			 (as the Sch., though the Ms. gives <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄκνον</span>). (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄτλος, ὀτλέω,
				ὀτλήμων</span> seem to be cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάλας, τλῆναι, τλήμων</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
